 .

Software: The programming languages, frameworks, and other software components that will be used 
 .

System Interfaces: How the different components of the system will interact with each other and with external systems 
 .

Data: The structure of the data, how it will be stored (e.g., in SQL or NoSQL databases), and how it will flow through the system 
 .

The design phase typically includes creating diagrams, mockups, and other documentation to explain the data flow and how components will interact 
 . This blueprint ensures that the development team has a shared understanding of the system's structure before writing any code 
 .

Understanding the Ecosystem: Whole-Program Analysis and Dependency Mapping
